{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks everyone for being here. As we all know, the customer-notification service needs a production message-streaming platform before its next integration milestone, and we're down to two finalists: KafkaCloud and StreamGrid. Both passed our benchmark of 20,000 messages per second with sub-250-millisecond median delivery latency, so on raw performance they're comparable. The draft architecture currently recommends StreamGrid based on simpler operational setup and an initial capacity estimate of four brokers. Since this is my decision to own, I want to make sure we go through the proper sign-off process — backend, support engineering, security, and FinOps — before I record anything. I'd like to hear from each of you on your respective areas of concern so we can make a well-rounded call. Who'd like to start?"}
```

