{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF4", "text": "I need to share something from the FinOps side. When I reconciled the cloud account this morning, I found that we already have existing KafkaCloud reserved-capacity credits that cover exactly six production brokers through the service's first year. StreamGrid has no equivalent credit. I should note that the draft architecture's four-broker estimate hasn't been amended to reflect this — but from a cost perspective, KafkaCloud would be fully covered for six brokers for the first year, while StreamGrid would be a net-new expense. This is a significant cost factor the group should weigh alongside the other concerns that have been raised."}
